• What design features would allow component upgrades without compromising structural or aesthetic integrity?
• How can product architecture be standardized across generations to maintain backward compatibility?
• Which components are most prone to technological obsolescence and should be prioritized for upgrade capability?
• What business models could incentivize manufacturers to design for upgradability rather than replacement cycles?
• How can users be guided to recognize upgrade opportunities and make informed upgrade decisions?
• What role does modular design play in supporting both upgrades and eventual material recovery?